  "question": "Can the failed homogeneous inequality D>=2A be replaced by an affine volume-uniform virial bound strong enough to control the actual BT Gibbs expectation of the half action-density weight?",
  "answer": "Yes. On every connected finite q-regular graph, grouping each vertex by the sign of r=s-q and using convexity and superadditivity of x log x gives D>=2A-N*q^2*(1+log(q)/4). For q=8, the rational certificate log(8)<21/10 yields D>=2A-(488/5)N. Gibbs radial integration by parts then gives, at lambda=2/5, E[A/N]<=1222/25 and E[sqrt(1+A/N)]<=sqrt(1247)/5 uniformly in volume. This closes the annealed action-density factor, but not the independent orthogonal-Hessian/curvature gate or the actual H^-1 moment.",
